# Local change to agnes

Upstream: https://github.com/kgabis/agnes (MIT)

One change only, and it is a no-op unless the including build opts in:

* An `AGNES_HOT` macro is defined near the top, empty by default.
* Nine functions on the per-cycle path are tagged with it: `agnes_tick`,
  `cpu_tick`, `ppu_tick`, `cpu_read8`, `cpu_read16`, `cpu_write8`,
  `ppu_read8`, `ppu_write8` and `scanline_visible_pre`.

`src/agnes_amalgam.c` defines `AGNES_HOT` to `IRAM_ATTR`, which places those
functions in the ESP32-P4's internal instruction RAM instead of running them
through the flash cache. `ppu_tick` alone is called about 89,000 times per
frame, so its fetch path dominates.

Nothing else is modified. With `AGNES_HOT` undefined the file is byte-for-byte
equivalent to upstream in behaviour and still builds on a host with no ESP
headers, which is how the ROMs were verified before any of this reached
hardware.
